      "id": 1,
      "text": "Haughton began as a railroad town in 1884 when the Vicksburg, Shreveport & Pacific Railroad built a station there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Haughton,_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In its first year, the Haughton depot shipped about 3,000 bales of cotton, supporting six businesses, boarding houses, and sawmills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
